{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Gift a Membership | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
<meta name="description" content="Give Mere Orthodoxy to someone who would value it. Choose one month to one year, add a note, and pick the day it arrives. Gift memberships never auto-renew." />
<meta property="og:title" content="Gift a Membership" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Give Mere Orthodoxy to someone who would value it. Choose one month to one year, add a note, and pick the day it arrives. Gift memberships never auto-renew." />
<meta property="og:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Gift a Membership" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Give Mere Orthodoxy to someone who would value it. Choose one month to one year, add a note, and pick the day it arrives. Gift memberships never auto-renew." />
<meta name="twitter:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- custom-gift: the /give/ chooser.

     Two products, two very different mechanics:

     1. Gift a membership (1/3/6/12 months) runs on GHOST'S NATIVE gift
        subscriptions. The CTA opens Portal at the `gift` route. Portal
        collects the recipient, the note, and the delivery date itself,
        so this page carries NO form for it. The recipient redeems by
        email and their term starts on the day they claim it.

     2. Lifetime ($995) cannot run on Portal, which has no concept of a
        one-time or perpetual purchase. It keeps the custom
        mo-membership checkout and now lives on its own page at
        /give/lifetime/ (custom-gift-lifetime.hbs).

     `data-portal="gift"` is a real Portal route (it match-cases `gift`
     alongside signin/account/offers). Portal enumerates [data-portal]
     ONCE at init, so this anchor must stay in the served HTML and must
     never be injected by script. Note also that Portal's handler bails
     silently if gift subscriptions are switched off site-wide in Ghost
     admin: it calls preventDefault() first, so the href is not a
     fallback and the button would simply go dead. If this CTA ever
     stops responding, check Settings first, not this template. --}}

<main class="membership membership-support">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Gift a Membership</p>
      <h1 class="page-hero-headline"><span class="highlight">Share Mere&nbsp;Orthodoxy</span> with someone who would value it.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Gift memberships never auto-renew. Your recipient gets an email with your note, claims it whenever they like, and is never asked for a card.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cards">

        {{!-- data-card-cta: membership-cards.js makes the whole card
             fire its CTA. Carried over from the pricing cards, where
             the heatmap recorded more dead clicks on benefit rows than
             real clicks on the button. Its INTERACTIVE list already
             excludes [data-portal], so forwarding to the Portal anchor
             below is safe and does not double-fire. --}}
        <article class="card card-member is-featured" data-card-cta data-hm-goal="gift-card">
          <span class="card-flag">Most Popular</span>
          <h2 class="card-label">Membership</h2>
          <div class="card-price">
            <span class="price-interval price-lead">Starts at</span>
            <span class="price-amount" data-full="$10">$8</span>
            <span class="price-interval">/month</span>
            <s class="price-was" data-sale-only><span class="visually-hidden">was </span>$10</s>
          </div>
          <p class="card-subtext" data-full="One month, three, six, or a full year">20% off through February 28</p>
          <p class="card-pitch">Choose the length, write a note, and pick the day it lands in their inbox.</p>
          <a
            class="btn btn-primary"
            href="#gift-form"
            data-hm-goal="gift-checkout"
          >Gift a Membership</a>
          <p class="btn-tagline">Never renews. No card from them.</p>
          <ul class="benefits">
            <li>The quarterly print journal, mailed to their door</li>
            <li>Digital archive of every past journal issue</li>
            <li>Private Discord community of serious readers</li>
            <li>Ebook and online event library</li>
            <li>Monthly Mailbag from Jake Meador</li>
            <li>The full archive, including 20+ years of essays</li>
            <li>Audio versions of every article</li>
            <li>Ad-free experience and the Member Dashboard</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card card-lifetime" data-card-cta data-hm-goal="gift-lifetime-card">
          <h2 class="card-label">Lifetime</h2>
          <div class="card-price">
            <span class="price-amount">$995</span>
          </div>
          <p class="card-subtext">One-time payment</p>
          <p class="card-pitch">For a reader you want to keep in Mere&nbsp;Orthodoxy for good, and who should have Trevin Wax's book on the shelf.</p>
          <a
            class="btn btn-dark"
            href="/give/lifetime/"
            data-hm-goal="gift-lifetime"
          >Gift a Lifetime Membership</a>
          <p class="btn-tagline">One-time. No renewal.</p>
          <ul class="benefits">
            <li><strong>Everything in Membership, plus:</strong></li>
            <li>A copy of Trevin Wax's The Lord Is My Light: A Liturgy for Daily Prayer</li>
            <li>Access that never expires</li>
            <li>Two annual memberships to give away</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

      </div>

      {{!-- YEAR-END GIFT CHECKOUT (2026-11-13). Gift memberships are 20%
           off through the year-end campaign. Ghost refuses Offers on
           gifts ("Offers cannot be applied to gift subscriptions"), so
           the discount is a second paid tier, "Gift Membership"
           (slug gift-membership, $8/mo, $80/yr), hidden from Portal.
           Portal's own gift picker only lists visible tiers, so this
           form posts the same request Portal sends to Ghost's members
           API with that tier's id. Ghost prices it, takes payment in
           Stripe, sends the gift email and handles redemption.

           RENEWAL: a recipient who continues after their gift pays the
           gift tier's price on the day they continue. mo-gift's scheduled
           job raises the tier to $10/$100 at GIFT_SALE_ENDS (midnight
           Central, March 1, 2027), and gift-checkout.js swaps every
           [data-full] price on this page at data-sale-ends, the same
           instant. Change the two together.

           The prices below are written out because a hidden tier is not
           in the Content API. Change them with the tier. To end the
           sale for good, restore the Portal CTA above (data-portal="gift")
           and remove this section. After March 1 the form keeps working at
           full price, so nothing breaks if that waits. --}}
      <section class="gift-checkout" id="gift-form" aria-labelledby="gift-form-title">
        <h2 class="gift-checkout-title" id="gift-form-title">Gift a Membership</h2>
        <form class="gift-checkout-form" method="post" data-gift-checkout data-gift-tier="6af751e9a28c1600017e7d61" data-sale-ends="2027-03-01T06:00:00Z" novalidate>
          <fieldset class="gift-checkout-group">
            <legend class="gift-checkout-legend">How long</legend>
            <div class="gift-lengths">
              <label class="gift-length"><input type="radio" name="duration" value="12" checked /><span class="gift-length-name">One year</span><span class="gift-length-price"><span data-full="$100">$80</span> <s data-sale-only><span class="visually-hidden">was </span>$100</s></span></label>
              <label class="gift-length"><input type="radio" name="duration" value="6" /><span class="gift-length-name">Six months</span><span class="gift-length-price"><span data-full="$60">$48</span> <s data-sale-only><span class="visually-hidden">was </span>$60</s></span></label>
              <label class="gift-length"><input type="radio" name="duration" value="3" /><span class="gift-length-name">Three months</span><span class="gift-length-price"><span data-full="$30">$24</span> <s data-sale-only><span class="visually-hidden">was </span>$30</s></span></label>
              <label class="gift-length"><input type="radio" name="duration" value="1" /><span class="gift-length-name">One month</span><span class="gift-length-price"><span data-full="$10">$8</span> <s data-sale-only><span class="visually-hidden">was </span>$10</s></span></label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="gift-checkout-group">
            <legend class="gift-checkout-legend">How it arrives</legend>
            <div class="gift-delivery">
              <label class="gift-delivery-option"><input type="radio" name="deliveryMethod" value="email" checked /> We email it to them on the day you choose</label>
              <label class="gift-delivery-option"><input type="radio" name="deliveryMethod" value="link" /> You get a link to hand over yourself</label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <div class="gift-checkout-group" data-gift-email-fields>
            <div class="gift-checkout-row">
              <label class="gift-field"><span>Their name <span class="gift-field-hint">(optional)</span></span><input type="text" name="recipientName" maxlength="191" autocomplete="off" /></label>
              <label class="gift-field">Their email<input type="email" name="recipientEmail" maxlength="191" autocomplete="off" /></label>
            </div>
            <label class="gift-field">Send it on<input type="date" name="deliveryDate" data-gift-date /></label>
            <label class="gift-field"><span>Your note <span class="gift-field-hint">(up to 250 characters)</span></span><textarea name="personalMessage" maxlength="250" rows="3"></textarea></label>
          </div>

          <div class="gift-checkout-row">
            <label class="gift-field">Your name<input type="text" name="buyerName" maxlength="191" autocomplete="name" /></label>
            <label class="gift-field" data-gift-buyer-email>Your email<input type="email" name="customerEmail" maxlength="191" autocomplete="email" /></label>
          </div>

          <noscript><p class="gift-checkout-note">Checkout needs JavaScript. Email ian@mereorthodoxy.com and we will set up your gift by hand.</p></noscript>
          <p class="gift-checkout-error" role="alert" data-gift-error></p>
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-solid btn-primary gift-checkout-submit" data-hm-goal="gift-checkout-submit">Continue to payment</button>
          <p class="gift-checkout-note">You pay through Stripe. Gift memberships never renew.</p>
        </form>
      </section>

      {{!-- The two products behave differently at the moment of giving,
           and that difference is the thing buyers get wrong. Say it
           plainly rather than letting them find out by email.

           These are h2 so all four headings on the page are siblings.
           As h3 they parsed as subsections of the Lifetime card, which
           is the last h2 above them. .gift-note-heading sets its own
           family/size/margin and the theme has no base heading rule, so
           the level is an outline change only, not a visual one.

           The address claim below is kept honest by a Ghost setting,
           not by theme code: the paid tier's welcome_page_url is
           /complete-membership/, whose first step is the mailing
           address, so a redeemer lands on it. If that setting is ever
           cleared in Ghost admin, this sentence becomes false. --}}
      <div class="gift-notes">
        <div class="gift-note">
          <h2 class="gift-note-heading">How a membership gift arrives</h2>
          <p>We email your recipient on the day you choose. They claim it with their name and email address, and the clock starts then, so a year given at Christmas runs to the following Christmas. If they never claim it, the gift expires after a year and you can ask us for a refund.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gift-note">
          <h2 class="gift-note-heading">About the print journal</h2>
          <p>Every gift includes the print journal, a one-month gift included. We ask your recipient for a mailing address when they claim the gift, so you do not need to know it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gift-note">
          <h2 class="gift-note-heading">If something goes wrong</h2>
          <p>Email <a href="mailto:ian@mereorthodoxy.com">ian@mereorthodoxy.com</a> and we will sort it out by hand. That covers a gift that will not start, a wrong address, a recipient who never got the email, and a date you want changed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <script src="{{asset "js/page/membership-cards.js"}}"></script>
  <script src="{{asset "js/lib/safe-redirect.js"}}"></script>
  <script src="{{asset "js/page/gift-checkout.js"}}"></script>
</main>
